layout_mode = 2
text = "There is a picture of a pet on the right side of the page.
The name of this pet is the next part of the secret code.

There is a specific formatting rule to follow to get the name right:
- not “horse,” but \"Horse\"
- not “elephant,” but “Elephant”
- not “him,” but “Him”
I think you see the logic behind this.

If the photo of the pet appears reversed, its name must be as well. In that case, the formatting looks more like “nositbE”, \"daB\", or \"dlihC\" ."
autowrap_mode = 3

